        "credit": "Richard Mortel from Riyadh, Saudi Arabia",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "description": "The Hamar (also spelled Hamer) are an Omotic community inhabiting southwestern Ethiopia. The Hamar are known for their unique custom of \"bull jumping,\" which initiates a boy into manhood. First, female relatives dance and invite whipping from men who have recently been initiated; this shows their support of the initiate, and their scars give them a right to demand his help in time of need. The boy must run back and forth twice across the backs of a row of bulls or castrated steers, and is ridiculed if he fails.",
        "width": 6000,
        "height": 4000,
        "quality_tier": 0,
